  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Transportation obligated $522M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Transportation recorded 1,925 contract awards for the period, with an average award size of $271K. Obligations fell 96.3% year over year. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Fiscal-year history shows a sharp decline from prior years: FY22 was $8B, FY23 was $8.7B, FY24 was $8.6B, FY25 was $9B, and FY26 was $14.1B. Engineering Services is the largest NAICS category so far in FY2027 to date at $110M, followed by Telecommunications Resellers at $95.1M and Computer Systems Design Services at $41M. HARRIS CORPORATION is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $95.1M, followed by CROWLEY GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. at $43.2M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $30.8M. This snapshot captures partial-year obligations and the largest categories and contractors receiving funds so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Transportation's FY2027 contract activity?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $522M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Transportation recorded 1,925 awards with an average award size of $271K. Obligations fell 96.3% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Transportation's top buys and suppliers so far this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Engineering Services leads NAICS categories at $110M, followed by Telecommunications Resellers at $95.1M and Computer Systems Design Services at $41M. HARRIS CORPORATION is the top vendor at $95.1M, followed by CROWLEY GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. at $43.2M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $30.8M. Several other service and tech categories appear in the top 10, including Ship Building and Repairing at $40.9M and Computing Infrastructure Providers at $32.9M."
      }
    ]
